{
 "id": "HT-PR-04 (prune: a root that is, lies inside or holds a protected path refuses the whole run and deletes nothing; identity by device and inode, NFC text for missing parts; a missing protected path still protects)",
 "needs": [
  "symlinks"
 ],
 "layer": "H",
 "owner": "skills",
 "note": "0.1.17 prune_protected_roots (settings file only) and --protect DIR: before anything is listed, every root prune reads or writes (handoff_root, disposable_root, the old default folders, each --root, the cache state folder) is compared with each protected path as real paths (~ expanded, links resolved, a missing path through its longest existing folder) by whole /-separated parts. equals, inside or contains refuses (exit 3, REFUSED: protected-root, each root and protected path named, no plan, nothing deleted, in the dry run and with --apply); a sibling with a shared text prefix does not; an entry that is not an absolute path refuses too; an empty list changes nothing; a plugin option in the environment cannot replace the file value. Identity (0.1.17 review): existing ancestors compare by device and inode, so an NFD spelling of an NFC folder and a macOS firmlink alias (/System/Volumes/Data...) refuse, also with --apply and a real plan from an unguarded dry run (the file stays); a root at or above the macOS join point (/System/Volumes/Data, /System/Volumes) holds a protected folder under it; a missing tail compares as NFC, case-folded text; with no usable identity (a test process replaces the identity sub, as a native Windows perl leaves it) the text compare alone decides; an entry's .. behind a link resolves as the kernel reads it; a folder swapped for a link into a protected folder after the check (a test wrapper, race.pl, swaps it) is neither deleted from nor rmdir-ed, and no MANIFEST row reads pruned for a file still there; --apply with a list that touches no root deletes and marks the row pruned only after the delete.",
 "now": "2026-11-08T12:00:00+03:00",
 "tz": "Etc/GMT-3",
